From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mapc_sync: not-measured is not a measurement
Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>

Two columns in the agent row carry a sentinel that reads like data.

The root node has no upstream, and its upstream_bssid is all zeros. Written
out as "00:00:00:00:00:00" it looks like an address, joins like an address,
and is indistinguishable from one. That is the same class of defect that
took the controller down on 5. 9., where an all-zero AL-MAC was treated as
an address and 473 854 log lines later the box was reset by its watchdog.
The view already turns it into NULL for the UI, which is the tell: the
value was never wanted, only tolerated.

est_thput_ul / est_thput_dl carry 0xFFFFFFFF when the agent does not know.
EasyMesh spends the maximum as its unknown marker, so stored as a number it
becomes the largest throughput in the table - and anything that picks a path
by throughput picks the node it knows least about. Measured 2026-09-06 on
five nodes: four agents carried 4294967295 in est_thput_dl and 0 in ul.

Both become NULL. Nothing else changes: the readers already handle NULL,
and a value that was never measured now says so instead of pretending.

Verify: on a live mesh, `select almac, upstream_bssid, est_thput_dl from
agent` must show NULL for the root's upstream and for every unknown
estimate - never 00:00:00:00:00:00 and never 4294967295.
--- a/src/db/mapc_sync.c
+++ b/src/db/mapc_sync.c
@@ -152,9 +152,29 @@
 	mapdb_bind_text(st, 5, caps);
 	mapdb_bind_int(st, 6, depth);
 	mapdb_bind_int(st, 7, n->ul_type);
-	mapdb_bind_text(st, 8, upbssid);
-	mapdb_bind_int(st, 9, n->est_thput_ul);
-	mapdb_bind_int(st, 10, n->est_thput_dl);
+	/* A zero upstream BSSID is not an address - it is the root having no
+	 * upstream at all. Written out as "00:00:00:00:00:00" it reads like a
+	 * real value and joins like one, which is the same class of defect that
+	 * took the controller down on 5. 9. (an all-zero AL-MAC treated as an
+	 * address). NULL says "none", and every reader already handles it.
+	 */
+	mapdb_bind_text(st, 8, hwaddr_is_zero(n->upstream_bssid) ? NULL : upbssid);
+
+	/* 0xFFFFFFFF is the agent saying "I do not know" - EasyMesh spends the
+	 * maximum as its unknown marker. Stored as a number it becomes the
+	 * LARGEST throughput in the table, so anything choosing a path by
+	 * throughput chooses the node it knows least about. Measured 2026-09-06:
+	 * four of five agents carried it. Not-measured is not a measurement.
+	 */
+	if (n->est_thput_ul == 0xFFFFFFFFu)
+		mapdb_bind_null(st, 9);
+	else
+		mapdb_bind_int(st, 9, n->est_thput_ul);
+
+	if (n->est_thput_dl == 0xFFFFFFFFu)
+		mapdb_bind_null(st, 10);
+	else
+		mapdb_bind_int(st, 10, n->est_thput_dl);
 	mapdb_bind_int(st, 11, n->scan_supported);
 	mapdb_bind_int(st, 12, n->sta_count);
 #if (EASYMESH_VERSION >= 6)
